# Git Conventions

Solo developer project — keep it simple. Use **Conventional Commits** format.

## Commit format

```
<type>: <short description>
```

## Types

| Type | Use when |
|------|----------|
| `feat` | New functionality or agent |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `refactor` | Code change with no behavior change |
| `chore` | Config, deps, tooling, infra |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `test` | Adding or fixing tests |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |

## Examples

```
feat: add LLMBudgetService evaluate method
fix: stack_detector fails on repos without package.json
refactor: extract FileClassifier from ContextBuilder agent
chore: add postgresql-table-design skill
docs: update architecture to Clean Architecture + DDD
test: add unit tests for budget decision logic
```

## Branching (optional, for bigger changes)

```
feat/stack-detector
fix/budget-overflow
refactor/context-builder-classifier
```

For small changes: commit directly to `main`.
